8️⃣Eight community dogs, who were loved and cared for by local feeders within the Army Cantonment in Mhow, were brutally caught by local pig catchers, allegedly on the instructions of the RWA Chairman, Col Akshay Khanna. They were trussed up, beaten severely, then transported 42 km away and dumped on the Indore highway.

When they were found, two were still alive. One has been taken to a shelter in Indore and will be brought back to his location upon recovery. The other, broken and terrified, fled.
It is shocking and saddening that civilised members of a disciplined organisation would resort to such illegal and cruel behaviour for no logical reason. What does this say about India?

A complaint has been filed, and accountability is being sought through the Army and police authorities. 
